## Review conclusion

The plane regression is now treated as a producer-authority problem, not another isolated transition predicate.

Current control flow conflates an authoritative producer being **not applicable** with that producer **rejecting** an applicable input. Both become `phaseFront.succeeded == false`, after which a different generic seed/trace/proposal producer runs automatically. Completion diagnostics can then overwrite the typed phase-front failure.

The exact production plane also uses preprocessing state absent from the passing reconstructed fan tests. A proven semantic inconsistency exists where phase-front transport treats relief edges as hard barriers even when `reliefBarriersEmbedded == false`.

